This directory contains a modified, audited source distribution maintained by
the pi-config project. It is not the unmodified npm package. The upstream source
is pinned to commit 356ea76836d04bcd2e9cbc09b289d5f18f732c65 (tag v3.5.0).

Material local changes include explicit approval for arbitrary custom Node.js
workflow code; rejection of hidden nested scripts; built-in workflow
precedence and default-off keyword triggering;
reviewed public-network-only web transport; restricted deep-research tools;
project-agent trust checks; fail-closed worktree and toolset handling; safe
run identifiers; removal of repository-local legacy state; private state-file
permissions; and hardened Git revision arguments. Full provenance and policy
are recorded in package.json, README.md, and SOURCE-PATCHES.md.

Custom workflow scripts remain arbitrary same-user Node.js code after the user
approves the displayed script. Node's vm API is not a security sandbox.
